# Reference Project Rule (strict)

All code in this repository MUST follow the patterns used in the reference
project:

**`/Users/d2118370gmail.com/Workspace/v0-interview-gym-ui-main`**

## Required Workflow (before writing any code)

1. **Check existing implementations** in this repo (`lib/`, `services/`,
   `services/dao/`, `app.js`, route handlers, `ios/**/*.swift`).
2. **Identify the closest matching pattern** in the reference project —
   look at `services/apiClient.ts`, `services/sessionService.ts`,
   `services/dao/sessionDao.ts`, `lib/trial.ts`, `lib/utils.ts`,
   `lib/auth-errors.ts`, `app/api/*/route.ts`, and `lib/__tests__/*.test.ts`.
3. **Reuse the existing structure and abstractions.**
   Do not invent a new layer, naming scheme, or error shape when an
   equivalent already exists.

## Rejection Rule

**Reject any solution that introduces a new pattern unless explicitly
required** (e.g. a capability the reference project has no equivalent for,
and the user has confirmed the new pattern is acceptable).

If you are tempted to introduce a new pattern:
- First state the closest existing pattern you considered.
- Explain exactly why it cannot be reused.
- Ask the user before proceeding.

## Non-Negotiables

- Layered architecture: route handler → `services/<feature>Service.js` →
  `services/dao/<feature>Dao.js`. Pure helpers (no I/O) live in `lib/`.
- ESM only (`import` / `export`), no trailing semicolons, double-quoted
  strings, `??` for nullish defaults.
- Every exported symbol gets a JSDoc (`/** ... */`) block describing
  **intent and constraints**, not the code.
- Tagged logs: `console.error("[API <route>]", e)`, `console.log("[server] ...")`.
- Tests in `lib/__tests__/*.test.js` (unit) and `test/*.integration.test.js`
  (integration), both using `node:test`.

See `.cursor/rules/backend-style.mdc` and `.cursor/rules/ios-style.mdc`
for concrete code patterns.
